From: Escapement
Subject: [PATCH] mfd: axp20x: keep the AXP2101's supplies when no IRQ is wired

Without an interrupt line, axp20x_device_probe() deliberately swaps in
axp_regulator_only_cells, with the comment "IRQs are required by some
drivers". For the AXP2101 that silently drops the battery and USB supplies:
the PMIC binds, logs "AXP20X driver loaded", and /sys/class/power_supply stays
empty. Nothing reports an error, which is what makes it hard to notice.

This board cannot use the IRQ yet. GPIO7 has no pull-up configured in pinctrl
and nothing external holds it, so a LEVEL_LOW interrupt on it storms and hangs
the boot (see patches/kernel/0003). That leaves the PMIC without an interrupt,
and therefore with no supplies at all.

Set cells_no_irq for the AXP2101 so the full cell set is used regardless,
matching what AXP806 already does. A sub-driver that genuinely needs an IRQ
then fails its own probe -- a visible, contained failure -- instead of every
supply disappearing at once with no message.

Verified: after this the boot logs

    axp20x-battery-power-supply axp20x-battery-power-supply: DMA mask not set
    axp20x-i2c 0-0034: AXP20X driver loaded

and still reaches buildroot login.

--- a/drivers/mfd/axp20x.c
+++ b/drivers/mfd/axp20x.c
@@ -1427,6 +1427,17 @@
 		axp20x->cells = axp2101_cells;
 		axp20x->regmap_cfg = &axp2101_regmap_config;
 		axp20x->regmap_irq_chip = &axp2101_regmap_irq_chip;
+		/*
+		 * Without an interrupt line axp20x_device_probe() falls back to
+		 * axp_regulator_only_cells, which drops the battery and USB
+		 * supplies entirely -- observable as an empty
+		 * /sys/class/power_supply even though the PMIC bound fine.
+		 * This board's IRQ pin is not pulled up, so no interrupt is
+		 * wired; keep the supplies and let any driver that truly needs
+		 * an IRQ fail its own probe instead of losing them all.
+		 */
+		nr_cells_no_irq = ARRAY_SIZE(axp2101_cells);
+		cells_no_irq = axp2101_cells;
 		break;
 	case AXP803_ID:
 		axp20x->nr_cells = ARRAY_SIZE(axp803_cells);
